### Variable Definitions
@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000/api

### 1. Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Accept: application/json

### 2. Create Valid Lead 1 (Alice Johnson)
# @name createLead1
POST {{baseUrl}}/leads
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Alice Johnson",
  "email": "alice.johnson@example.com",
  "phone": "+1 (555) 019-2834",
  "company": "Acme Innovations",
  "source": "WEBSITE",
  "status": "NEW"
}

### 3. Create Valid Lead 2 (Bob Smith)
# @name createLead2
POST {{baseUrl}}/leads
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bob Smith",
  "email": "bob.smith@techcorp.com",
  "phone": "+1-555-432-1098",
  "company": "TechCorp Solutions",
  "source": "REFERRAL",
  "status": "QUALIFIED"
}

### 4. Create Lead with Invalid Email (Expect 400 with details)
POST {{baseUrl}}/leads
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Invalid Email Lead",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "phone": "+1 (555) 123-4567",
  "company": "Test Co",
  "source": "WEBSITE"
}

### 5. Create Lead with Missing Required Fields (Expect 400 with details)
POST {{baseUrl}}/leads
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "X"
}

### 6. Create Duplicate Lead Email (Expect 409 Conflict)
POST {{baseUrl}}/leads
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Alice Duplicate",
  "email": "alice.johnson@example.com",
  "phone": "+1 (555) 999-8877",
  "company": "Another Co",
  "source": "LINKEDIN"
}

### 7. List All Leads (Default: page 1, limit 10, sort createdAt desc)
GET {{baseUrl}}/leads
Accept: application/json

### 8. List Leads with Custom Pagination and Sorting
GET {{baseUrl}}/leads?page=1&limit=1&sortBy=name&order=asc
Accept: application/json

### 9. Search Leads by Name (Case-insensitive)
GET {{baseUrl}}/leads?search=alice
Accept: application/json

### 10. Filter Leads by Status
GET {{baseUrl}}/leads?status=QUALIFIED
Accept: application/json

### 11. Combined Search and Status Filter
GET {{baseUrl}}/leads?search=techcorp&status=QUALIFIED
Accept: application/json

### 12. Get Lead by ID (Replace with an existing ID from Create response)
GET {{baseUrl}}/leads/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Accept: application/json

### 13. Get Lead with Invalid UUID Format (Expect 400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/leads/not-a-valid-uuid
Accept: application/json

### 14. Get Lead with Nonexistent UUID (Expect 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/leads/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
Accept: application/json

### 15. Update Lead (Replace with valid ID)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/leads/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "CONTACTED",
  "company": "Acme Innovations Global"
}

### 16. Delete Lead (Replace with valid ID - Expect 204)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/leads/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 17. Verify Deleted Lead is Gone (Expect 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/leads/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Accept: application/json
